 "literal": "Whether a country / or whether a forest / Whether a lowland / or whether a highland / In whichever place men are good / In that place you are good, may you prosper, O land!",
 "translation": "Whether you are a cultivated country or a wild forest, whether you are a low valley or a high hill, wherever the men are good, there you are good too. May you prosper, O land!",
